  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 250 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nFriday a more northerly flow will be over the Panhandles, which is\ngenerally less favorable for storm development, however residual\noutflow boundaries and perhaps a subtle wave may move through in\nthe afternoon to trigger storm development. If a storm develops it\nwill likely track due south. Outflow boundaries will most likely\nreside in the north given where the best chances of storms are on\nThursday, but if we do get the MCS noted in the short term that\ncould lead to outflow boundaries that could hold more over the\nCanadian River Valley and I-40 corridor. But overall storm motion\nwill be about 5-15 mph to the south on Friday. Saturday through \nTuesday the high pressure will continue to linger just east of the\nFour Corners and keep us under more of that north to \nnortheasterly flow. Pops for the extended for the most part will \nbe less than 15 percent. There is a hint that the ridge may start \nto break down early in the work week, but confidence is still very\nlow < 15% at this point. \n\nWeber",
